            <ArticleTitle>[A man with atypical appendicitis].</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>A3432</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>A 43-year-old man presented with acute left-sided middle and lower abdominal pain. He was diagnosed with 'left-sided acute appendicitis with non-rotation of the colon'. This is a rare and usually asymptomatic congenital anomaly.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
